matters to customers who care

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:40.110
about privacy and security.

00:06:40.110 --> 00:06:42.490
And that's almost
every single customer.

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:44.070
One of the reasons
we're able to go

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:46.140
do this is because
we do something

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:48.060
that's called cold potato.

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:50.220
Now you might ask,
what is cold potato?

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:51.450
Cold potato is this.

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:54.120
Basically, it means
that what Google does

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:58.200
is we hold onto a data
packet as long as possible

00:06:58.200 --> 00:06:59.837
before it gets to the end user.

00:06:59.837 --> 00:07:01.920
And we do that because we
want to provide security

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:05.490
and privacy, but we also want to
make sure it's very performant.

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:07.170
When you look at
other cloud providers,

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:10.160
generally what they do
is they play hot potato.

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:12.660
They get your packet, and they
want to pass it off to an ISP

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:13.860
as soon as possible.

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:15.540
And it might be
an ISP that might

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:20.130
have the reliability, the
privacy, and quality of service

00:07:20.130 --> 00:07:22.560
that you might get
inside Google Cloud.

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:24.900
I actually think highly
performant networks

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:26.790
are really, really important.

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:28.530
If you go talk to
Niantic as an example--

00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:30.414
